    "title": "Quality Control (QC) Checklist",
    "format": "html",
    "content": "<ul>\n<li>✅</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Quality Control (QC) Checklist</h2>\n<h2>Revital Productions — Internal Use Only | Updated June 2026</h2>\n<p>PURPOSE: Every deliverable produced by Revital Productions must pass this QC checklist before it moves from Internal Review to Client Review in ClickUp. No exceptions. This checklist is the last line of defense before work reaches the client — if it doesn't pass QC, it goes back to production.</p>\n<p>WHO RUNS THIS: The account manager or designated QC reviewer — never the same person who produced the deliverable.</p>\n<p>WHERE TO LOG IT: The Hub's QC Checklist tool logs it automatically (reviewer, deliverable, round, result, date) when you save a review - no separate ClickUp comment needed. Still move the ClickUp task status to Client Review once it passes.</p><p>HOW TO USE: Run the Universal Checklist first (applies to every deliverable), then the service-specific checklist that matches what you're reviewing, both inside the Hub tool. Check every item. If anything fails, move the task back to In Production with a clear note on what needs to be fixed.</p>\n<h2>QC CHECKLIST INDEX</h2>\n<h2>Checklist When to Use</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Universal QC Every single deliverable — always run this first</li>\n<li>Social Media Content Posts, Reels, Stories, carousels for any platform</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Paid Ad Creative Facebook, Instagram,</h2>\n<h2>Google, TikTok, LinkedIn ads</h2>\n<h2>SEO Monthly SEO work, blog posts, on-page optimizations</h2>\n<h2>Email Marketing Newsletters, drip emails,</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Checklist</th>\n<th>When to Use</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>🔲 Universal QC</td>\n<td>Every single deliverable — always run this first</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>📱 Social Media Content</td>\n<td>Posts, Reels, Stories, carousels for any platform</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>📣 Paid Ad Creative</td>\n<td>Facebook, Instagram, Google, TikTok, LinkedIn ads</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>🔍 SEO</td>\n<td>Monthly SEO work, blog posts, on-page optimizations</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>Monthly Reports Client performance reports before delivery</h2>\n<h2>Run the Checklist</h2><p>Use the Hub's <strong>QC Checklist</strong> tool for the active client instead of working through this document by hand. It has the Universal Checklist plus all seven service-specific checklists (Social Media Content, Paid Ad Creative, SEO, Email Marketing, Website, Video &amp; Content Production, Monthly Reports) built in as an interactive, per-client checklist with a progress bar - and every completed review is automatically logged to that client's QC history (reviewer, deliverable, round, result, date), so there's no need to separately note it in a ClickUp comment.</p><p>Move the ClickUp task from Internal Review to Client Review once the tool shows it passed.</p><h2>QC FAILURE PROTOCOL</h2>\n<p>If a deliverable fails QC at any point, follow this process:</p>\n<h2>4. Move the task status back to In Production</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><ol start=\"5\">\n<li>Set a revised due date that still allows time for re-review before the client deadline</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><ol start=\"6\">\n<li>If the failure will cause a delay to the client delivery date — notify the account manager immediately so the client can be informed proactively</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li><ol start=\"7\">\n<li>Once fixes are made, the deliverable must go through the full QC checklist again — not just the failed items</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A deliverable that has failed QC twice on the same issues must be escalated to leadership before it is sent to the client.</p>\n<h2>QC LOG — HOW TO RECORD COMPLETION</h2>\n<p>After every QC review, add a comment to the ClickUp task in this format:</p>\n<h2>✅ QC COMPLETED</h2>\n<h2>Reviewer: [Your Name]</h2>\n<h2>Date: [Date]</h2>\n<h2>Deliverable: [Description]</h2>\n<h2>Round: [X of X]</h2>\n<h2>Result: PASSED / FAILED</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Notes: [Any notes — issues found, fixes requested, or \"All items passed\"]</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>QC Checklist Version 1.0 | Revital Productions | June 2026</h2>\n<p>This checklist must be completed for every deliverable before it reaches the client. No exceptions.</p>",
    "date": "2026-07-29",
    "category": "Core Operations"
