    "content": "<h2>💰 Invoice &amp; Billing SOP</h2>\n<h2>Owner: Operations</h2>\n<p>Trigger: 1st of every month or per contract billing schedule</p>\n<p>Key tools used in this SOP:</p>\n<p>🧾 ClickUp — CRM Deals list, Invoices &amp; Payments list in Finance &amp; Billing folder</p>\n<p><strong>Invoicing tool: QuickBooks</strong> — this is the confirmed system of record for all client invoices</p>\n<p>📧 Email Templates — Template #14 Invoice Send, Template #15 Overdue Invoice Follow-Up</p>\n<p>📞 Client Communication Policy — Part B for billing dispute escalation rules</p>\n<h2>Steps</h2>\n<h2>1. Review Active Clients (by the 1st)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Pull all active deals from ClickUp CRM with Billing status of Monthly or an upcoming installment (1 of</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>3 / 2 of 3 / 3 of 3)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm services delivered this month match what is being billed — cross-reference with the client's</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>📋 Scope of Work Log in the Legal folder</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Flag any Change Orders approved this month — add additional fees to the invoice</li>\n<li>Flag any clients where services were paused or cancelled mid-month — adjust invoice accordingly</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2. Generate Invoices (by the 2nd)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Create an invoice for each active client in <strong>QuickBooks</strong></li>\n<li>Include: services rendered, billing period covered, itemized line items, total amount due, and payment due date</li>\n<li>Set payment terms per the client's contract: Net 15 or Net 30</li>\n<li>Apply any approved discounts or credits</li>\n<li>Reference the client's signed SOW for exact service names and rates — match them exactly on the invoice</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>3. Send &amp; Log (by the 2nd)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Client name</li>\n<li>Invoice number</li>\n<li>Amount</li>\n<li>Date sent</li>\n<li>Due date</li>\n<li>Status: Sent / Paid / Overdue</li>\n<li>Update the Billing field in the client's CRM Deal record to reflect the current billing cycle</li>\n<li>Set Invoice Status to <strong>Sent</strong> in the Hub's 💳 Contract &amp; Invoice Tracker — this is what QBR Generator pulls for the Billing &amp; Contract section, so it needs to match ClickUp</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4. Track Payments</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update the 🧾 Invoices &amp; Payments task to Paid as soon as payment is received</li>\n<li>Update the Billing field in the CRM Deal record when an installment is paid (1 of 3 → 2 of 3, etc.)</li>\n<li>Set Invoice Status to <strong>Paid</strong> in the Hub's 💳 Contract &amp; Invoice Tracker to match</li>\n<li>Log the payment received date in the task comments</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>5. Follow Up on Overdue Invoices</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Day 1 overdue: Send Email Template #15 — Overdue Invoice Follow-Up — friendly tone, assume it was overlooked; set Invoice Status to <strong>Overdue</strong> in Contract &amp; Invoice Tracker</li>\n<li>Day 7 overdue: Send a second follow-up — slightly more direct, ask for a payment date</li>\n<li>Day 15 overdue: Escalate to leadership immediately — do not handle billing disputes independently per Client Communication Policy Part B</li>\n<li>Leadership will determine whether to pause services, issue a final notice, or make other arrangements</li>\n<li>Flag all overdue invoices in the client's CRM Deal record Comments with the date and amount</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Billing Rules</h2>\n<h2>Rule Standard</h2>\n<p>Invoice accuracy Always cross-reference against the signed SOW before sending</p>\n<p>Change Orders Must be added to the invoice in the same month</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Rule</th>\n<th>Standard</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Invoice accuracy</td>\n<td>Always cross-reference against the signed SOW before sending</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>paused without leadership approval</h2>\n<h2>Overdue threshold Escalate to leadership at Day</h2>\n<h2>15 — do not wait longer</h2>\n<p>Communication All billing communication uses Email Templates #14 and #15 — not the client portal</p>\n<p>Last updated: June 2026 | Owner: Revital Productions Operations</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Overdue threshold</th>\n<th>Escalate to leadership at Day 15 — do not wait longer</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Communication</td>\n<td>All billing communication uses Email Templates #14 and #15 — not the client portal</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
